# The Dockerfile copies src/, alembic/, pyproject.toml, uv.lock and README.md —
# about a megabyte. Without this file the build context was 509MB, because the
# daemon is handed the whole directory before the first COPY is evaluated:
# a 272MB host virtualenv (wrong platform, never used), 141MB of food photos
# and 23MB of licensed PDFs, transferred on every build.
#
# Deny by exclusion rather than by allowlist: a new source directory should
# reach the image by default, and a new pile of data should not.
#
# Patterns are `**/`-prefixed wherever the target can nest. Docker does NOT
# match the way .gitignore does: a bare `__pycache__/` matches only a
# top-level directory, so every nested one shipped anyway. That leak is
# invisible — the build succeeds and the Dockerfile's explicit COPY keeps the
# junk out of the image, so only the context size ever shows it.

# the host virtualenv: built for the host, rebuilt inside the image anyway
.venv/
**/*.egg-info/

# personal data that must never enter an image layer.
# papers/ is matched at any depth, like the .gitignore rule: the directory has
# already moved from the repo root to docs/ once, and a path-pinned rule would
# have stopped matching silently the next time.
data/
**/papers/
eval/photos/
eval/results/
eval/truth.csv
eval/dinnerware.json

# secrets. Settings reads these from the environment at runtime, never a layer.
.env
.local.env
**/*.env
!.env.example

# caches and history
.git/
.gitignore
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/

# nothing here changes the image, and each entry invalidates the cache
docs/
tests/
sql/
ops/
justfile
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
CLAUDE.md
**/*.md
!README.md

# macos
**/.DS_Store
